0002: the A830 KGSL base chip-id (ROCKNIX port), Mesa 27 form.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Taken from the ArmadOS image recipe for
stack compatibility (Mesa 26.2.3 applies the twin
`0002-add-a830-chip-id-mesa26.patch`), not authored here; origin ROCKNIX
(`patches/PATCHES.md`). Upstream: nothing to send for Mesa 27 - upstream already
carries all four A830 ids; only the 26.2.3 twin is a real change, not ours.
**Found:** inherited; the Mesa 27 re-export was done 19.11 (`docs/release.md`,
"Provenance").

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set and nothing to expect on an A740; the row is a no-op on Mesa 27.

## Summary

The ROCKNIX patch added three ids to Mesa 26.2.3, where `add_gpus()` had two.
Mesa 27 already lists all four (`0xffff44050000`, `0xffff44050001`, KGSL
`0x44050000`, KGSL `0x44050001`), so this form adds a second identical
`GPUId(chip_id=0x44050000, ...)` row, and the generated table matches on the first
one: effect zero. The row is kept so the file list stays what the image builds.
This patch is not "A830 support was added here".

## Evidence

One row in `add_gpus()` of `freedreno_devices.py`; the generated
`freedreno_dev_info.h` carries it. The published bundle and the bench ship tree
differ in exactly this line and nothing else, 94 EXACT either way
(`docs/release.md` provenance).

## Tests

What checks the change is that it must be inert on this device: 94 EXACT with and
without the row (matrix journal 24.3). A real A830 machine is the only thing that
would test it - NOT TESTED, none exists here.

## The change in this repo

One row, one hunk. The 26.2.3 form stays next to it unchanged because
`image-build/build.sh` applies that one. Revert: `git apply -R` with the file name
explicit.

## Related

`patches/PATCHES.md`; the `-mesa26` twin; `docs/release.md` provenance.

